issue_context.body:
Hello Developers!

_this is my first issue to Zephyr, or any other open source project! if i should put this somewhere else or I just do it wrong -- tell me please._

I have a problem with ADC over DMA on STM32F429i-DISC1 board running samples/drivers/adc sample. I get a hardfault on dma_config(), executing an undefined instruction (api->config()). I think that something is not fully initialized through the DT.

I had the same issue on a STM32G071 on my custom board on DMAMUX and I couldn't solve it, so I tried a SoC (F429) without the MUX, but the problem prevails. My workaround was to use HAL/LL for DMA temporarily, but I would like to switch back to Zephyr implementation whenever possible. Any suggestions are much appreciated. 

I include a debug screenshot, call stack and zephyr terminal output, together with the DTS overlay and prj.conf entries.

Specs: 
Board: STM32f429i-Disc1
Build: `west build -p -b stm32f429i_disc1 samples/drivers/adc`  
Debug and flash tool: JLink OCD
Development environment: VSCode + cortex-debug
ZephyrOS version: 3.5.0
SDK: 0.16.3_windows_x86_64

### prj.conf entries:
```
CONFIG_ADC=y
CONFIG_DMA=y
CONFIG_ADC_STM32_DMA=y
CONFIG_ADC_ASYNC=y
```

### Debug screenshot (VSCode + cortex-debug via JLink)

> **Note:** `api=dev->api;` while `dev` is 0x00! Therefore `api` struct contains nonsense, and calling a function from a pointer inside it will lead to provblems

![image](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/assets/71927208/68f477d6-7dd9-4033-a89a-6b2d27a11da3)


### Call Stack 
![image](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/assets/71927208/4e47df54-e15b-44fe-9ecc-44beceb7c8ba)

### Terminal screenshot
![image](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/assets/71927208/3ebcaa26-7c35-4cb5-96c7-47b28af09880)


...and is my DTS overlay
```
 / {
    zephyr,user {
        io-channels = <&adc1 1>;//<&adc1 2 &adc1 1>;
    };
};

&adc1 {
    #address-cells = <1>;
    #size-cells = <0>;
    status = "okay";
    pinctrl-0 = <&gpio_a6_analog>;
    pinctrl-names = "default";
    st,adc-prescaler = <4>;
    st,adc-clock-source = <SYNC>;
    dmas = <&dma2 0 0 (STM32_DMA_PERIPH_TO_MEMORY | STM32_DMA_PERIPH_16BITS) 0x00>;
    dma-names="adcdma";
    channel@1 {
        reg = <1>;
        zephyr,gain = "ADC_GAIN_1";
        zephyr,reference = "ADC_REF_INTERNAL";
        zephyr,acquisition-time = <ADC_ACQ_TIME_DEFAULT>;
        zephyr,resolution = <12>;
    };

};

&pinctrl {
    gpio_a6_analog: gpio_a6_analog {
        pinmux = <STM32_PINMUX('A',6,ANALOG)>;
    };
    status = "okay";
};


&dma2 {
    status = "okay";
};
``` 

Hope putting this issue may help someone in the future

p.s. Used screenshots instead of text logs because I put the same problem on Discord forum before, and this is rather a copy of the post I made
